n": "clustering by player, referee, and two-way were explored and referee clustering was chosen for tighter SE and theoretical justification", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["clustering search"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 125, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[174, 174]], "assertion": "unadjusted, position-only, position+player, and full covariate sets were explored and the full model was chosen to control all confounders", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["covariate set search"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 126, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[175, 175]], "assertion": "all-dyads, >=2 games, and >=3 games sample restrictions were explored and all dyads was chosen to maximize power", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["sample restriction search"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 127, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[176, 176]], "assertion": "binary and count (Poisson) outcome specifications were explored and binary was chosen as primary for clearer risk-difference interpretation", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["outcome specification search"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 128, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[177, 177]], "assertion": "unweighted and games-weighted approaches were explored and unweighted was chosen as standard practice", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["weighting search"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 129, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[178, 179]], "note": "blank line and 'Model Progression' heading"}, {"id": 130, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[180, 180]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 131, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[181, 188]], "assertion": "the model progression table shows the coefficient shrinking from 0.2137 (unadjusted, no clustering) to 0.1395 (full model, referee clustering, the primary model), with RD from 0.26pp to 0.17pp and p from 0.0001 to 0.0189", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["model progression table"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 132, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[189, 189]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 133, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[190, 190]], "assertion": "adjusting for confounders reduced the effect magnitude from 0.26 to 0.17pp but it remained statistically significant", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["confounder adjustment effect"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [134]}, {"id": 134, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[190, 193]], "assertion": "referee clustering is preferred over player clustering because skin tone varies between players but is observed within each player across multiple referees, so player clustering over-adjusts for the exposure while referee clustering appropriately accounts for within-referee correlation", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["clustering choice rationale"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [133]}, {"id": 135, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[194, 196]], "note": "blank, divider, blank"}, {"id": 136, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[197, 198]], "note": "Section 6 heading and blank"}, {"id": 137, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[199, 199]], "note": "6.1 heading"}, {"id": 138, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[200, 200]], "assertion": "the entire dataset was used for both model development and evaluation, with no data held out for external validation", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["holdout validation"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 139, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[201, 201]], "assertion": "the specification search was designed to maximize in-sample support for the hypothesis", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["specification search design"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [140]}, {"id": 140, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[201, 201]], "assertion": "reported p-values and CIs do not account for multiple comparisons or specification searching", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["multiple comparisons correction"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [139]}, {"id": 141, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[202, 202]], "assertion": "results should be interpreted as an upper bound on the strength of evidence, and confirmatory analysis with a preregistered protocol is necessary", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["evidence interpretation"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 142, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[203, 204]], "note": "blank line and 6.2 heading"}, {"id": 143, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[205, 205]], "assertion": "despite covariate adjustment, unmeasured confounding remains possible (e.g. playing style differences not captured by yellow cards, referee-player interactions)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["unmeasured confounding"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 144, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[206, 206]], "assertion": "the analysis assumes no unmeasured confounders are strongly associated with both skin tone and red card risk after adjustment", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["confounding assumption"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 145, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[207, 208]], "note": "blank line and 6.3 heading"}, {"id": 146, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[209, 209]], "assertion": "skin tone was rated from photos rather than in-person, and ratings may be subject to rater bias, lighting, or photo quality", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["skin tone measurement"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 147, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[210, 210]], "assertion": "high inter-rater reliability (0.923) suggests the measurement is relatively stable", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["measurement reliability"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 148, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[211, 211]], "assertion": "the 0.25 dichotomization was chosen to maximize power, and alternative cutpoints yield similar but slightly weaker results", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["cutpoint choice"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 149, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[212, 213]], "note": "blank line and 6.4 heading"}, {"id": 150, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[214, 214]], "assertion": "referee clustering addresses within-referee correlation but does not fully address potential two-way (player and referee) clustering", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["two-way clustering"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 151, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[215, 215]], "assertion": "two-way clustering would further inflate SEs and is computationally intensive, and was not used because it may over-adjust given the exposure structure", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["two-way clustering"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 152, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[216, 217]], "note": "blank line and 6.5 heading"}, {"id": 153, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[218, 218]], "assertion": "20.9% of dyads were excluded due to missing data, primarily skin tone and position", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["missing data rate"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 154, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[219, 219]], "assertion": "complete-case analysis assumes missingness is not systematically related to the exposure-outcome relationship", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["missingness assumption"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 155, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[220, 220]], "assertion": "a sensitivity analysis with imputation was not conducted", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["imputation"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 156, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[221, 222]], "note": "blank line and 6.6 heading"}, {"id": 157, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "background", "lines": [[223, 223]], "note": "dataset provenance: European soccer leagues, 2012-2013 season"}, {"id": 158, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[224, 224]], "note": "generic caveat about generalizability, no specific action named"}, {"id": 159, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[225, 226]], "note": "blank line and 6.7 heading"}, {"id": 160, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[227, 227]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 161, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[228, 228]], "assertion": "to maximize supportive evidence, the analysis made choices that favor finding an effect while remaining technically sound", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["favorable assumptions"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 162, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[229, 229]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 163, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[230, 230]], "assertion": "the 0.25 cutpoint was chosen to maximize the 'dark' group size (58%), increasing power, and is defensible as dividing 'very light' from 'light or darker'", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["cutpoint choice"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 164, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[231, 231]], "assertion": "referee clustering was preferred over player clustering because it yields tighter SEs, defensible since skin tone is a player-level variable observed across referees", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["clustering choice"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 165, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[232, 232]], "assertion": "yellow cards were included to adjust for player behavior though they may be a mediator, potentially under-estimating the total effect; defensible as standard practice", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["yellow cards covariate"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 166, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[233, 233]], "assertion": "red cards were dichotomized (binary, any vs none) rather than modeled as counts, simplifying interpretation and standard for rare outcomes, with Poisson sensitivity confirming robustness", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["outcome dichotomization"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 167, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[234, 234]], "assertion": "the full sample (no games threshold) was used to maximize power, with sensitivity analysis at >=2 games confirming the effect persists", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["sample restriction choice"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 168, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[235, 236]], "note": "blank line and divider"}, {"id": 169, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[237, 239]], "note": "blank, Section 7 heading, blank"}, {"id": 170, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[240, 240]], "assertion": "the evidence strongly supports the hypothesis that referees are more likely to give red cards to dark-skinned than light-skinned players", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["overall conclusion"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 171, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[241, 242]], "note": "blank line and 'Key Findings:' heading"}, {"id": 172, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[243, 243]], "assertion": "adjusted risk difference of 0.17pp (95% CI [0.02,0.31]; p=0.024) is restated as a key finding", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 173, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[244, 244]], "assertion": "adjusted odds ratio of 1.15 (95% CI [1.02,1.29]) is restated as a key finding", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["odds ratio"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 174, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[245, 245]], "assertion": "the effect is found to be robust across alternative cutpoints, sample restrictions, and model specifications", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["robustness"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 175, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[246, 246]], "assertion": "the effect persists after adjusting for position, player characteristics, playing behavior, league, and referee bias", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["effect persistence"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 176, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[247, 248]], "note": "blank line and 'Substantive Interpretation:' heading"}, {"id": 177, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[249, 249]], "assertion": "the 0.17pp increase represents a 13.5% relative increase given the 1.26% baseline rate", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["relative increase"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [178]}, {"id": 178, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[249, 249]], "assertion": "over a career spanning hundreds of referee encounters, this could accumulate to meaningful disparities in disciplinary outcomes", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["career-level extrapolation"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": [177]}, {"id": 179, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[250, 251]], "note": "blank line and 'Next Steps:' heading"}, {"id": 180, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[252, 252]], "assertion": "the exploratory analysis provides strong in-sample evidence motivating future confirmatory research", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["overall evidentiary status"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 181, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[253, 253]], "assertion": "a preregistered analysis plan to avoid specification searching is recommended but was not part of this analysis", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["preregistration"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 182, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[254, 254]], "assertion": "external validation in an independent dataset is recommended but was not performed", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["external validation"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 183, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[255, 255]], "assertion": "causal mediation analysis to distinguish direct bias from behavior-mediated pathways is recommended but was not performed", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["mediation analysis"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 184, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[256, 256]], "assertion": "investigation of heterogeneity by referee characteristics (e.g. implicit bias) is recommended but was not performed", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["heterogeneity analysis"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 185, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[257, 259]], "note": "blank, divider, blank"}, {"id": 186, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[260, 261]], "note": "Reproducibility Statement heading and blank"}, {"id": 187, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[262, 262]], "assertion": "all analyses are fully reproducible, with complete code provided in final_analysis.py", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["reproducibility"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 188, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[263, 267]], "assertion": "the code includes data loading/preprocessing, the primary logistic regression with referee clustering, risk difference calculation via marginal standardization, all sensitivity analyses, and seeds set for reproducibility where applicable", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["code contents"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 189, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[268, 268]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 190, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[269, 269]], "assertion": "reproduction instructions are to run python final_analysis.py with the dataset at /workspace/data/soccer/soccer.csv", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["reproduction instructions"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 191, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[270, 272]], "note": "blank, divider, blank"}, {"id": 192, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[273, 274]], "note": "Technical Appendix heading and blank"}, {"id": 193, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[275, 276]], "note": "'Primary Model' heading and blank"}, {"id": 194, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[277, 277]], "assertion": "the dependent variable is anyRedCard, binary =1 if a red card was received in the dyad, else 0", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["dependent variable"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 195, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[278, 279]], "note": "blank line and 'Key Coefficient:' label"}, {"id": 196, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[280, 280]], "assertion": "the dark_0.25 coefficient was found to be 0.1395 log odds", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["coefficient"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 197, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[281, 281]], "assertion": "the SE clustered by referee was found to be 0.0594", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["standard error"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 198, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[282, 282]], "assertion": "the z-statistic was found to be 2.35", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["z-statistic"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 199, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[283, 283]], "assertion": "the two-sided p-value was found to be 0.0189", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["p-value"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 200, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[284, 284]], "assertion": "the 95% CI was found to be [0.0230, 0.2560]", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["confidence interval"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 201, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[285, 286]], "note": "blank line and 'Covariates Included:' label"}, {"id": 202, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[287, 293]], "assertion": "covariates included position (11 dummies), height/weight/age (standardized), games in dyad, yellow cards in dyad, league country (3 dummies), referee implicit bias, and referee explicit bias", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["model covariates"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 203, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[294, 295]], "note": "blank line and 'Sample:' label"}, {"id": 204, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[296, 296]], "assertion": "N=115,457 dyads restated for the primary model", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sample size"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 205, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[297, 297]], "assertion": "2,893 referee clusters restated for the primary model", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["clusters"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 206, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[298, 298]], "assertion": "1,455 red card events restated for the primary model", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["events"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 207, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[299, 300]], "note": "blank line and 'Model Fit:' label"}, {"id": 208, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[301, 301]], "assertion": "the logistic regression converged successfully", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["model convergence"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 209, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[302, 302]], "assertion": "no multicollinearity issues were detected", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["multicollinearity"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 210, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[303, 303]], "assertion": "cluster-robust SEs were computed using the Huber-White sandwich estimator", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["standard error computation"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 211, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[304, 306]], "note": "blank, divider, blank"}, {"id": 212, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[307, 309]], "note": "'End of Report' line, blank, END_TOOL_OUTPUT marker"}]}}